% orcid-import.bib -- NOT part of the build. Import-only helper.
%
% Upload this file at https://orcid.org/my-orcid -> Works -> Add -> Import
% BibTeX, to register the conference papers and patents that have no DOI and
% therefore cannot reach ORCID through Search & Link.
%
% Safe to import: fetch_orcid.py only reads ORCID works that carry a DOI, so
% these entries land in your ORCID record without changing publications.bib,
% publications.tex, or the site. They stay sourced from manual.bib.
%
% Notes on ORCID's importer:
%   - @inproceedings maps to work type "Conference paper".
%   - The patents below use @misc, not @patent: @patent is not standard
%     BibTeX and is not in ORCID's supported type list, so it risks being
%     dropped on import. @misc imports reliably as work type "Other" --
%     change those two entries to "Patent" in the ORCID UI afterwards.
%   - ORCID stores only year granularity for these, so the full conference
%     dates in `note` are informational.
%   - Re-importing the same file creates duplicates in ORCID. Import once,
%     then edit in place.
%
% Keep this file in sync with the corresponding manual.bib entries; the
% citation keys match deliberately.

